cognoscentibus, 'the jury,' but also
of magistrates hearing a case, Iul. 38;
Claud. 15 and 33; Nero 15.

ludis, 'at the games,' abl. of time.
So gladiatoribus, Cic. Att. 2, 19, 3;
ludis et gladiatoribus ib. 1, 16.

exilivit for exiluit, a recurrence it
seems to an ancient form. Fest. 206 M.;
cp. saliere Verg. G. 2, 384.
